{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790521175,"nonce":"0lyBOKDZx6qzakKZcHbQwrkZ6bQ=","message":"Cause: on non-unix targets krio-fiber allocates a coroutine stack as a zero-filled Vec (stack.rs heap_stack), so each coroutine commits its whole 64 MB (coroutines.rs STACK_BYTES) up front. c_stack.lua nests about 200 coroutines, cstack.lua keeps 1000 alive; when the commit fails Rust aborts with a fast-fail, 0xC0000409. Whether it fails depends on what else the runner has committed, so at 17c83ed7 c_stack passed with warm-up on and failed with it off. A smaller stack does not fit: errors/stack_overflow.lua recurses to MAX_DEPTH inside a coroutine and overflows 1 MB on Linux. The fix is in krio-fiber: reserve the Windows stack with VirtualAlloc(MEM_RESERVE) and commit on demand behind a guard page, as the unix mmap path does. Until then errors/c_stack.lua is listed unix (branch fix/ci-platform-flakes, 6bb5a3c7).","files":null}]}